From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:04:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8180x-microsoft-surface-pro-x: Build
 on 7.3

The posted tree sets the PCIe 2 reset and wake GPIOs on its root port,
pcie2_port0, which sc8180x.dtsi only gains with commit dea048d7c7ce
("arm64: dts: qcom: sc8180x: Move PCIe phy and GPIOs to root port
node"). That commit doesn't apply to 7.3's Flex 5G and Primus trees, so
set them on the controller as perst-gpios and wake-gpios, as the Flex 5G
does in 7.3.

Also enable QUP wrapper 2, which the posted tree left out and which
uart13 (WCN3998 Bluetooth) and uart15 (the Surface Aggregator Module)
sit behind.

Suggested-by: Haipeng Lin <jimmie.lin@gmail.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261104070441.74127-3-val@packett.cool/
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-microsoft-surface-pro-x.dtsi    | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-microsoft-surface-pro-x.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-microsoft-surface-pro-x.dtsi
index 17fb01c..dd73ca7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-microsoft-surface-pro-x.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-microsoft-surface-pro-x.dtsi
@@ -745,6 +745,9 @@
 	// XXX: pcie1 and pcie2 are multi'd together, for now use just one
 	num-lanes = <2>;
 
+	perst-gpios = <&tlmm 102 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pcie1_default_state>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 
@@ -783,9 +786,8 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-&pcie2_port0 {
-	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 102 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+&qupv3_id_2 {
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &remoteproc_adsp {
-- 
2.56.0

